*> Test of 40-1 section 3 (The menu model; T0993): isValidSlotIndex (-1, -999 and every index below the count, no lower bound), the ContainerInput
*> id decoding (out of range is PICKUP), the quick-craft button mask, and the appended player inventory slots (3.3).
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-MENU-40-1-3.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 COPY CORESTATE.
 COPY BESTATE.
 COPY PROTO.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(8192).
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-EDIT2               PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-EDIT3               PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-EDIT4               PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-I                   BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-LEN                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-IDX                 BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-CAPACITY            BINARY-LONG VALUE 4096.
 01 WS-ZERO                BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
 01 WS-TYPE10              BINARY-LONG VALUE 10.
 01 WS-E1 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E2 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E3 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E4 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E5 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E6 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E7 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E8 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E9 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E10 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E11 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-E12 PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-A BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-B BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-C BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-D BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-F BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-G BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-H BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-J BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-K BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-K32 PIC X(32).
 01 WS-KEY2 PIC X(32).
 01 WS-L BINARY-LONG.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-1§3 menu model: isValidSlotIndex accepts -1, -999, indexes below the count and any negative number, not the count itself" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 63 TO WS-D
     MOVE -1 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-VALID-SLOT" USING WS-A WS-D WS-B
     MOVE -999 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-VALID-SLOT" USING WS-A WS-D WS-C
     MOVE 62 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-VALID-SLOT" USING WS-A WS-D WS-F
     MOVE 63 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-VALID-SLOT" USING WS-A WS-D WS-G
     MOVE -5 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-VALID-SLOT" USING WS-A WS-D WS-H
     MOVE WS-B TO WS-E1
     MOVE WS-C TO WS-E2
     MOVE WS-F TO WS-E3
     MOVE WS-G TO WS-E4
     MOVE WS-H TO WS-E5
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E5) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "1 1 1 0 1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK

     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-1§3 menu model: ContainerInput ids 0 to 6 decode as themselves, 7 and -1 as PICKUP (0)" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 0 TO WS-D
     PERFORM VARYING WS-A FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL WS-A > 6
         CALL "MENU-INPUT-DECODE" USING WS-A WS-B
         ADD WS-B TO WS-D
     END-PERFORM
     MOVE 7 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-INPUT-DECODE" USING WS-A WS-C
     MOVE -1 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-INPUT-DECODE" USING WS-A WS-F
     MOVE WS-D TO WS-E1
     MOVE WS-C TO WS-E2
     MOVE WS-F TO WS-E3
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "21 0 0" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK

     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-1§3 menu model: quick-craft button 5 is header 1 type 1; 6 is header 2 type 1; 10 header 2 type 2; mask recombines" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 5 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-QC-MASK" USING WS-A WS-B WS-C WS-D
     MOVE 6 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-QC-MASK" USING WS-A WS-F WS-G WS-H
     MOVE 10 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-QC-MASK" USING WS-A WS-J WS-K WS-L
     MOVE WS-B TO WS-E1
     MOVE WS-C TO WS-E2
     MOVE WS-D TO WS-E3
     MOVE WS-F TO WS-E4
     MOVE WS-G TO WS-E5
     MOVE WS-H TO WS-E6
     MOVE WS-J TO WS-E7
     MOVE WS-K TO WS-E8
     MOVE WS-L TO WS-E9
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E5) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E6) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E7) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E8) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E9) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "1 1 5 2 1 6 2 2 10" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK

     MOVE "acceptance US12 40-1§3 menu model: with 27 own slots the main inventory is slots 27 to 53 (inventory 9 to 35) and the hotbar 54 to 62 (inventory 0 to 8); own slots are not inventory" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE 27 TO WS-D
     MOVE 27 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-APPEND" USING WS-D WS-A WS-B
     MOVE 53 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-APPEND" USING WS-D WS-A WS-C
     MOVE 54 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-APPEND" USING WS-D WS-A WS-F
     MOVE 62 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-APPEND" USING WS-D WS-A WS-G
     MOVE 26 TO WS-A
     CALL "MENU-APPEND" USING WS-D WS-A WS-H
     MOVE WS-B TO WS-E1
     MOVE WS-C TO WS-E2
     MOVE WS-F TO WS-E3
     MOVE WS-G TO WS-E4
     MOVE WS-H TO WS-E5
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E1) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E2) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E3) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E4) " " FUNCTION TRIM(WS-E5) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     MOVE "9 35 0 8 -1" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK

     GOBACK.

 CHECK.
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-TEXT TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.
 END PROGRAM TEST-MENU-40-1-3.

 COPY CORETEST.
